   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <ab>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Seefeldstrasse 73</name> <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>
                            <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zürich</name>
                        </addrLine>
                    </address>
                </ab> <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>
                        </salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>        	A friend of ours suggests that perhaps the <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">Rationalist Press</seg> or some similar society might print <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">the book</rs>
                        </seg> for you. <rs type="person" key="joyc82">My husband</rs> is <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">recovering</seg> very slowly. The eye is still bleeding but there are no <choice>
                            <sic>complication</sic>
                            <corr>complications</corr>
                        </choice>.</p> <closer>
                        <salute>       	Yours sincerely</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="barn84">                    	Nora Joyce</name>
                        </signed> </closer> </div> </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The Rationalist Press Association promoted freethought and in the early 20th century published a substantial number of books advocating agnosticism, evolution, and a skeptical view of Christianity. The identity of the “friend” who recommended the Press is unknown. Weaver tried to interest the Rationalist Press’s printers in the early episodes of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> for publication in <name type="work" key="W_THEEGOIST">The Egoist</name>, but had no success (Firth 179).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">
                    <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>.</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">JJ had undergone an eye operation after suffering a severe attack of glaucoma on the evening of August 18 (<name type="work">JJ</name> 417).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
